# React Router 7 Routing Config

`app/routes.ts` is the source of truth for routing. Two strategies: programmatic (preferred when route shape is known up front) and filesystem (faster scaffolding for many routes).

## Programmatic via @react-router/dev/routes

```ts
// app/routes.ts
import { type RouteConfig, index, route, layout, prefix } from "@react-router/dev/routes";

export default [
  index("routes/home.tsx"),
  route("about", "routes/about.tsx"),

  layout("routes/_marketing.tsx", [
    route("pricing", "routes/pricing.tsx"),
    route("blog/:slug", "routes/blog.$slug.tsx"),
  ]),

  ...prefix("api", [
    route("health", "routes/api/health.ts"),
  ]),

  route("*", "routes/not-found.tsx"),
] satisfies RouteConfig;
```

- `index(file)` mounts at the parent path.
- `route(path, file, children?)` adds a URL and a UI segment.
- `layout(file, children)` adds a UI wrapper without a URL segment.
- `prefix(seg, children)` prepends a URL segment without a UI wrapper.

## Filesystem via @react-router/fs-routes

```ts
import { type RouteConfig } from "@react-router/dev/routes";
import { flatRoutes } from "@react-router/fs-routes";
export default flatRoutes() satisfies RouteConfig;
```

`flatRoutes()` is async; await or return its promise. Default `rootDirectory: "routes"`.

## File-name conventions (flat routes)

| File                                    | URL                              | Notes                                       |
|-----------------------------------------|----------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| `_index.tsx`                            | `/`                              | Root index, not `index.tsx`                 |
| `about.tsx`                             | `/about`                         |                                             |
| `products._index.tsx`                   | `/products`                      | Index of the products layout                |
| `products.$pid.tsx`                     | `/products/:pid`                 | `$` prefix for dynamic                      |
| `products.$pid.edit.tsx`                | `/products/:pid/edit`            | Dots become slashes inside `routes/`        |
| `docs.$.tsx`                            | `/docs/*`                        | `$.tsx` is splat (catch-all)                |
| `_layout.tsx`                           | (none)                           | Pathless layout (leading underscore)        |
| `($lang).about.tsx`                     | `/about` or `/:lang/about`       | `(...)` is optional segment                 |
| `users.tsx` + `users.profile.tsx`       | `/users/profile` nested in `users.tsx` | Default nesting                       |
| `users_.profile.tsx`                    | `/users/profile`                 | Trailing `_` breaks out of `users.tsx` layout |
| `[sitemap.xml].tsx`                     | `/sitemap.xml`                   | `[...]` escapes special characters          |

## Refused patterns

- `app/routes/index.tsx` for `/`. Must be `_index.tsx`.
- `app/routes/products.[id].tsx` (Next.js bracket). Must be `products.$id.tsx`.
- `app/routes/docs.*.tsx`. Must be `docs.$.tsx`.
- Defining the same path in both `flatRoutes()` and `route(...)`: v7 errors with a duplicate-route message.

## Resource routes

Routes that return raw HTTP `Response` (RSS, sitemap, JSON API) must export only `loader` and/or `action`, no `default`. See `react-router-route-modules.mdc` for the full shape.

